# FlightConn — Optional user configuration
# ==========================================
# Copy this file to deploy.env only if you need FAA SWIM recent activity data.
#
#   cp deploy.env.example deploy.env
#
# deploy.env is listed in .gitignore and must NEVER be committed.
#
# The main app (Route Map, Route Opportunity Finder, Airline Health) runs
# fully without this file. FAA SWIM data is optional.
#
# ── How SWIM auto-detection works ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# setup.sh detects whether SWIM is ready automatically:
#   - If FAA_USER, FAA_PASS, and at least one QUEUE_* are set → SWIM enabled.
#   - If any of those are blank or missing → SWIM disabled, main app runs normally.
#
# No flags to set. Just fill in your credentials and queues.
# The broker URL, probe settings, and TLS configuration are handled internally.

# ── FAA Credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Leave blank to run FlightConn without FAA SWIM recent activity.
# Issued by FAA after a completed SWIM Service Access Agreement (SAA):
#   https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/technology/swim
# Never commit these values.
FAA_USER=
FAA_PASS=

# ── SWIM Queue Names ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Queue names are assigned by FAA after account setup.
# At least one queue is required for SWIM recent activity to run.
# SFDPS  — System Flight Data Processing System (en-route/oceanic data)
# STDDS  — SWIM Terminal Data Distribution System
# TFMS   — Traffic Flow Management System (departure/arrival/flow data)
QUEUE_SFDPS=
QUEUE_STDDS=
QUEUE_TFMS=
